&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harbor&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;/span&gt;looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Intapp Implementation Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to lead the design, configuration and delivery of Intapp solutions for legal-sector clients. You will work with client stakeholders across IT, Risk and Compliance, Finance and legal teams to turn business needs into secure, practical solutions across the matter lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone with substantial experience implementing and enhancing Intapp products in a law-firm environment. You will take ownership of complex workstreams, guide technical decisions and support other members of the delivery team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end Intapp implementation work, from discovery and requirements through solution design, configuration, testing, deployment and post-go-live support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and enhance workflows, forms, rules and application configurations for client and matter intake, conflicts, risk and compliance, time recording or related processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise clients on solution options, product capabilities, design trade-offs and implementation approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and support relevant Intapp products, such as Intapp Intake, Conflicts, Open, Time, Walls, Flow and Integrate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and oversee integrations with legal finance, document management and other business systems, including integration testing and defect resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead workshops with business and technical stakeholders; document requirements, process flows, functional designs and technical specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and coordinate system testing, user acceptance testing, data validation, training, deployment and business readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex issues and work with client teams and Intapp support to resolve product or implementation problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve workflows, controls, data quality and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance to junior engineers and contribute to delivery standards, documentation and estimates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support upgrades, migration planning and cloud readiness where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least five years of hands-on experience implementing, configuring or significantly enhancing Intapp products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering Intapp solutions in a law firm or comparable professional-services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven participation in multiple implementation or major enhancement projects, with responsibility for solution design and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of one or more Intapp products, such as Intake, Conflicts, Open, Time, Walls, Flow or Integrate. Depth in a core product is essential; experience across several products is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing workflows and translating Risk, Compliance, Finance or legal business requirements into technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with integrations between Intapp and other enterprise or legal-sector systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence leading workshops, managing stakeholders and explaining technical choices clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning or carrying out testing, deployments, upgrades and post-go-live support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, documentation and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intapp cloud migration or cloud readiness work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legal finance or document management platforms such as Aderant or iManage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL, APIs, reporting tools or integration platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conflicts management, ethical walls, information barriers, client due diligence or AML workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile delivery, project governance or mentoring other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How success will be measured:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will deliver reliable Intapp solutions that meet agreed business and control requirements, communicate risks and decisions clearly, and leave clients with supportable configurations and useful documentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;x_ContentPasted0&quot;&gt;About Us:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;x_ContentPasted0&quot;&gt;Harbor is the preeminent provider of expert services across strategy, legal technology, operations, and intelligence. Our globally integrated team of 900+ strategists, technologists, and specialists navigate alongside our clients – leading law firms, corporations, and their law departments – to provide essential resources and invaluable insights. Anchored in a rich heritage of deep knowledge, steadfast relationships, and mutual respect, our unwavering dedication lies in shaping the future of the legal industry and fostering enduring partnerships within our community and ecosystem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;x_ContentPasted0&quot;&gt;Harbor is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, civil union status, national origin, ancestry, age, parental status, disabled status, veteran status, or any other legally protected classification, in accordance with applicable law.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harbor&lt;/strong&gt; is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Director &lt;/strong&gt;to join our dynamic Enterprise Solutions – Financial Systems team. We work with leading vendors, allowing clients to benefit from our product-specific expertise, strategic insight, and market perspective. We serve as trusted advisors and experienced delivery leaders, partnering with clients to improve financial systems and operations, support data-driven decision making, and deliver technology initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Financial Systems leadership team, you will lead complex client engagements, build trusted executive-level relationships, and deliver strong outcomes across a portfolio of projects and accounts. You will advise law firm leaders on financial systems, operating practices, and technology investments while overseeing project delivery and team leadership. You will also contribute to sales pursuits in partnership with Harbor’s business development leaders.&amp;nbsp;As a Director, you will lead and mentor Managers, Consultants, and Associate Consultants within the Financial Systems practice, with accountability for team performance, consulting delivery, and client experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time position that can be worked remotely in the United States or United Kingdom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Job Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to law firm executive leadership, providing guidance on financial systems, operating practices, and technology roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex financial systems engagements, including implementations, integrations, optimization projects, and ongoing operational improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep subject matter expertise in legal financial management platforms (e.g., Elite 3E and related ecosystem solutions), advising clients on industry practices, system capabilities, and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain executive-level client relationships, serving as a senior point of contact and escalation resource and supporting strong, lasting client partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help clients address targeted process and organizational improvement opportunities as part of broader financial systems engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review key project deliverables and provide executive oversight, including solution designs, implementation plans, testing approaches, training plans, governance frameworks, and, where relevant, assessments, business cases, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop Managers and consulting team members through coaching, career development guidance, performance feedback, and leadership support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee resource management and workforce planning across multiple client engagements to support efficient utilization, delivery quality, and employee development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in business development in partnership with Harbor’s sales and practice leaders. Contribute subject matter expertise, client relationship context, solution development, proposal responses, and client presentations; sales ownership, targets, and accountability remain with designated business development leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop service offerings, methodologies, accelerators, and intellectual property that strengthen Harbor’s Financial Systems capabilities and market differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor legal industry, technology, and market trends to identify relevant opportunities, risks, and recommendations for clients and Harbor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with software vendors, implementation partners, and industry organizations to support client delivery and the practice’s service offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support practice financial management and operational planning, including engagement forecasting, margin management, and resource planning. Provide input to pipeline reviews as requested by practice and business development leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Harbor’s overall growth strategy by identifying cross-functional opportunities and collaborating with leaders across service lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion consulting excellence, ensuring adherence to Harbor methodologies, quality standards, and client delivery best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain personal billable utilization consistent with leadership expectations while helping the team meet utilization, profitability, and delivery expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience, Education and Other Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in legal technology, professional services, consulting, or financial systems, including significant experience leading financial systems implementations and optimization programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in law firm financial systems, including implementation, integration, optimization, governance, and change management; experience with strategy, assessment, or selection work is beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build trusted relationships with C-level and senior executive stakeholders and influence business and technology decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and the ability to connect technology investments and operational improvements to measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading multiple concurrent client engagements, managing project teams, overseeing budgets, and mitigating delivery risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to business development through client relationship support, proposal development, solution design, and participation in sales pursuits. Direct sales ownership or revenue-generation accountability is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership experience managing consulting teams, developing talent, and building high-performing teams in a client-service environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, facilitation, and storytelling skills, with the ability to translate complex technical concepts into executive-level recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making capabilities, with experience improving financial systems and related business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of project and program management principles, including resource planning, financial management, governance, quality assurance, and stakeholder management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing methodologies, service offerings, practice collateral, and thought leadership content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to balance hands-on engagement leadership with strategic practice responsibilities and collaborative participation in business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive, entrepreneurial mindset with a passion for innovation, continuous improvement, and building client value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office applications (Excel, PowerPoint, Word, and Visio) and collaboration tools including Outlook, Teams, and SharePoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;x_ContentPasted0&quot;&gt;About Us:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;x_ContentPasted0&quot;&gt;Harbor is the preeminent provider of expert services across strategy, legal technology, operations, and intelligence. Our globally integrated team of 900+ strategists, technologists, and specialists navigate alongside our clients – leading law firms, corporations, and their law departments – to provide essential resources and invaluable insights. Anchored in a rich heritage of deep knowledge, steadfast relationships, and mutual respect, our unwavering dedication lies in shaping the future of the legal industry and fostering enduring partnerships within our community and ecosystem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;x_ContentPasted0&quot;&gt;Harbor is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, civil union status, national origin, ancestry, age, parental status, disabled status, veteran status, or any other legally protected classification, in accordance with applicable law.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence, and guest-centered ethos that define Airbnb. This team’s mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping independent, boutique hotels easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Account Executive, you will be responsible for converting leads into net‑new supply to support new-market launches and at pace to hit quarterly goals. Working the full sales funnel, you will proactively turn cold leads into warm sales opportunities helping to build the Hotels category’s market presence in the process through collaboration with other teams. This includes partnering, strategizing, and running daily operations directly with independent, boutique hotels , and ensuring that Airbnb sources&amp;nbsp; the best hotel inventory available to our guests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Paris (hybrid, 2 days a week in the office).&amp;nbsp; It will start off as a 12-month FTC with the potential for conversion depending on individual performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet and exceed KPIs by owning the performance and success of assigned region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect new potential hotels through external research, networking, and use of Airbnb tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Securing new hotels involves targeted sales strategies and negotiating and closing the deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops acquisition strategies and scalable, localised supply strategies for established and emerging markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertly position and communicate Airbnb’s value proposition to new partners via phone, email, and in-person&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add net new hotels by qualifying and moving leads through the funnel as quickly as possible, achieving defined quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find supply in and launch new markets: Own market launches including supporting lead generation and coordinating cross functionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hotel onboarding as needed from won sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively promote and build strong relationships with hotels by demonstrating comprehensive knowledge of our platforms and confidently pitching their value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience, preferably in a fast growing startup tech or hospitality company working in sales and/or account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous hospitality experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in both English and French.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM required; Proficiency in Salesforce, Gong and other scalable AI Sales prospecting tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to get things done with constantly changing priorities, projects and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, organizational, and analytical skills, detail-oriented but moves fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to establish strong relationships with and influence partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity to balance day-to-day responsibilities with longer-term strategic execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a quick learner and you’re fearless about doing whatever it takes to get the job done, even if it means making mistakes along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel up to 25-30% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Airbnb and travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We’ll Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for variable incentive pay, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The On-Target Earnings (“OTE”) range for this role is €98,000 to €115,000 gross per year, which includes a split of 80% (base pay) / 20% (variable incentive).&amp;nbsp;Of this OTE amount, the annual gross base salary range is €78,400 to €92,000.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The OTE reflected on this job posting is the target cash compensation a candidate could earn in a year if they achieve 100% of their performance or sales goals. The variable incentive is not guaranteed and is governed by the terms of Airbnb’s Hotels Variable Compensation Plan (the “Plan”). The actual payouts depend on performance against targets set under the “Plan” and may be higher or lower than the range listed on this job posting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is looking for a Marketing &amp;amp; CRM intern to join the Experiences team in Paris for a 6-month internship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the person in charge of Demand for Paris Experiences, alongside Marketing, Growth and Product Management partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experiences let guests step into the real life of a destination: cook with a local chef, explore a hidden neighborhood with a historian, discover Paris through the eyes of the people who live there. Paris is one of our most iconic and competitive markets, and our job on the Demand side is to make sure the right guests find the right Experience at the right moment, whether they are visiting Paris or live nearby.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a curious, organized and data-friendly student who loves the craft of CRM and Operational Marketing: a sharp brief, a well-built email, a smart audience, and an analysis that tells us what to do next. You are comfortable juggling several campaigns at once, working with different teams, and turning numbers into clear recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support the Paris Experiences Demand lead on the day-to-day CRM and marketing activity that drives bookings. You will see a campaign from the first brief to the final analysis, and you will own your own projects along the way. During your internship, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Run email campaigns end to end&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write briefs for email campaigns (audience, objective, key messages, timing) and coordinate with copy, design and CRM partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute campaigns through our internal tools and planning process, including setup, QA and send follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze results after each send (opens, clicks, bookings, incrementality) and share clear learnings and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Support listing promotion and audience targeting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze cohorts of guests (new vs. returning, local vs. traveler, International vs Domestic) to understand behavior over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build simple, readable dashboards and recurring reports to select and prioritize listings based on quality, availability, performance and fit with the campaign&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Market and Supply teams to make sure what we promote is bookable and best-in-class&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn insights into concrete recommendations for audiences, timing and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Follow local activations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational support and follow-up on field campaigns such as flyering, partnerships, events or more: briefing, logistics, timing, partners and results tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help measure what works locally and recommend future iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The intern experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you will be part of a team where you contribute to real projects with real business impact. Your manager, your team and our wider employee community will strive to be superhosts to you during your internship. We provide the support, mentorship and hands-on experience you need to learn quickly and make an impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get a front-row seat on how a global marketplace builds demand for a destination, with real ownership from day one: your campaigns go live and your analyses shape decisions. You’ll do it alongside a team that cares about craft, curiosity and human connection. You can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Marketing, Market Management and Acquisition partners to deliver projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present your analyses and recommendations to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek and give feedback throughout the internship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in the Experiences and broader Airbnb community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current student or recent graduate&lt;/strong&gt; (degree completed within the last 12 months) from a leading business school, engineering school or equivalent program in France, looking for a 6-month internship starting in January 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French and English&lt;/strong&gt;, with excellent written communication: you can write a clear brief and a clear recap. You also have an eye for great copy and for what makes a message feel human&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong interest in marketing, CRM or growth&lt;/strong&gt;, and in travel, hospitality or community-driven products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious about data and performance metrics&lt;/strong&gt;, with an interest in using insights and quantitative analysis to evaluate campaigns, track performance, and inform decision-making. Experience with Claude or other AI tools to work faster and smarter is a must-have.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented&lt;/strong&gt;, able to manage several campaigns and deadlines in parallel, and to follow up until everything is done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A collaborative mindset &lt;/strong&gt;and the confidence to work with people across teams, from Marketing to Product to Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have work authorization for France. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of this position, the successful applicant will need to be based in Paris, France to be able to conduct their work. Interns can expect to spend half of their time at the office and half working remotely with exact dates as agreed upon by the hiring manager. Additional in-person attendance for team meetings or offsites may be required as needed. Please note we are unable to provide relocation or visa sponsorship for this position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our commitment to inclusion &amp;amp; belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp; This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
